{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Abraham gave gifts.</b> They said in the chapter חלק that 'names' means he transmitted to them the act of mentioning the Explicit Name while in bodily impurity, so that it would not harm them. And even today there are Ishmaelites who are expert in the Name and mention it in impurity. And it troubled R. Moshe: how could a man and an important righteous one like Abraham teach the Name to wicked men? Therefore R. Ya'akov bar R. Nachman explained: 'name of impurity' means the name of the demons — that one adjures them by their masters, the officers appointed over them, to do whatever one wishes, like the book Bil'ad; and it is called 'name of impurity' after the spirit of impurity, as we say in tractate חגיגה: one who sleeps in a graveyard so that a spirit of impurity rests upon him. A hint to this: for מתנות is written defective vav, and its gematria equals למדם להשביע השדים ('he taught them to adjure the demons'). From R. Moshe."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:59.315297771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}